# Every text file is checked out with CRLF, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says. The release ZIP
# packs files as the checkout wrote them, so their line endings are part of its bytes: left to each
# machine's Git settings, two checkouts of one tag would give two ZIPs. The repository stores LF.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# cmd.exe misreads labels and `goto` in a batch file with LF endings, wherever it was unpacked.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
